# RepoPrompt Portable v@@VERSION@@

This release publishes the immutable multi-architecture image `@@IMAGE@@`.

## Current contract

- Portable software `@@SOFTWARE_VERSION@@`; tool schema `@@SCHEMA_VERSION@@` on all seven MCP tools.
- `context_builder` supports local `clarify` and provider-backed `plan|review|pro_edit` over the explicit selection; `pro_edit` returns read-only instructions and never writes, delegates, executes, or applies.
- `oracle_send` remains limited to `chat|question|plan|review`, always attaches the explicit selection, and fails closed before HTTP when provider context is incomplete.
- Review calls accept bounded caller-supplied `review_diff`; `oracle_send` also accepts `clarify_handoff`. Both are untrusted evidence sent to both concurrent lanes.
- Surf-compatible bearer authentication, top-level `reasoning_effort`, compound model IDs such as `gpt-5.6-sol-xhigh`, structured completion/error/recovery metadata, and timeouts through 3600 seconds are supported.
- The direct CLI supports atomic, no-overwrite, mode-0600 `--export-jsonl` artifacts.

## Assets

- `container-digests.json`: immutable index/platform/config digests.
- `repoprompt-portable-v@@VERSION@@-linux-{amd64,arm64}.docker.tar.gz`: verified Docker-loadable images.
- `repoprompt-portable-linux-{amd64,arm64}.spdx.json`: SPDX SBOMs.
- `docker-compose.yml` and `run-hardened.sh`: digest-pinned hardened launch examples. They optionally forward `OPENCODE_API_KEY` for the default OpenCode provider; leave it unset for explicit Surf configuration.
- `SHA256SUMS` and `SHA256SUMS.sigstore.json`: checksums and keyless signature bundle.
- `RELEASE_POLICY.txt`: immutability and rollback policy.

## Verify before use

```bash
sha256sum --check SHA256SUMS
cosign verify-blob \
  --bundle SHA256SUMS.sigstore.json \
  --certificate-identity 'https://github.com/dsebban/repoprompt-portable/.github/workflows/publish-container.yml@refs/tags/v@@VERSION@@' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  SHA256SUMS

gh attestation verify repoprompt-portable-v@@VERSION@@-linux-amd64.docker.tar.gz \
  --repo dsebban/repoprompt-portable

IMAGE="$(python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open("container-digests.json")); print(d["image"]+"@"+d["index_digest"])')"
cosign verify \
  --certificate-identity 'https://github.com/dsebban/repoprompt-portable/.github/workflows/publish-container.yml@refs/tags/v@@VERSION@@' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  "$IMAGE"
gh attestation verify "oci://$IMAGE" \
  --repo dsebban/repoprompt-portable \
  --signer-workflow dsebban/repoprompt-portable/.github/workflows/publish-container.yml
```

The content assets, including both SBOMs and archives, are covered by `SHA256SUMS` and their GitHub build-provenance attestations. `SHA256SUMS` is itself protected by the verified Sigstore bundle and exact workflow identity.

## Rollback

Release tags `v@@VERSION@@`, `@@VERSION@@`, and `sha-<full-commit>`, plus digests and release assets, are immutable. `latest` is the only movable tag. A rollback may move `latest` only to a previously verified and signed digest; verification failures never fall back to unsigned publication. A digest implicated in credential exposure remains ineligible until the external credential owner confirms revocation or rotation.
